{
"name": "valve_ep2_rocket",
"note": "Episode Two's rocket as it stands in White Forest's silo (ep2_outland_11), in the silo piece's own frame (anchor 1824 -9936 -1728, the shaft's axis on the pit floor, the same as valve_ep2_silo): stage 1 (347 to 747) with its three engines, stage 2 (731 to 939), stage 3 (874 to 1263), the nose (rocket.mdl, 1238 to 1629) and the hatch (rocket_hatch, a prop_dynamic). About 97 across from the axis at most. With Valve's steam round it: three jets from the engines' exhaust (on from the start, 85 long, grey) and two small vents at the nose (on), and the big jet at the nose (steamjet_rocket_1, here rocket_nose_jet, off: Valve's story starts it). The hatch at the top is kept open (the owner, 22 November: \"keep the little door at the top of the rocket open\"): a logic_auto plays the hatch model's 'closing' sequence at spawn and HoldAnimation keeps its last frame (Valve's door_rocket_hatch, a nodraw func_door_rotating, plays 'closing' when it opens, so that sequence is the hatch opening). Left out: its lighting origins, the hatch's func_door_rotating (nodraw), the welder's sparks and glow (parented to a citizen welder in Valve's map). Valve's launch (ep2_outland_12a: rocket_low on a func_tracktrain) is not in it.",
